{
  "id": "Mtkt3nxbvGsGyxqi",
  "meta": {
    "instanceId": "8443f10082278c46aa5cf3acf8ff0f70061a2c58bce76efac814b16290845177"
  },
  "name": "Coaching Session to Action Plan (Zoom Recap, Homework Tracker & Nudges)",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "d96fff36-3df5-4387-9d9d-5b8ed6631c3b",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1120,
        -112
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 744,
        "height": 932,
        "content": "# Coaching Session to Action Plan\n\nWriting recaps after every call eats a coach's evening, and clients forget half of what they agreed to by the next session. This workflow turns each Zoom recording into a recap, homework and a running tracker, then checks in with the client until the work gets done.\n\n## How it works\nWhen Zoom finishes a recording it calls the webhook. The workflow answers Zoom's security handshake, matches the meeting to a client in your sheet and skips sessions it has already handled. It uses Zoom's transcript when there is one and falls back to Whisper on the audio. GPT turns the conversation into a personal summary, wins, 2-5 homework tasks with due dates and a progress score. The client gets a recap email with the coach in CC, the session goes into a log and each task lands in the Homework Tracker. A second flow runs daily, finds tasks due soon or slightly overdue, and sends each client a single friendly check-in.\n\n## Setup steps\n1. Create a Google Sheet with Clients, Session Log and Homework Tracker tabs (columns are in the section notes) and paste its ID into every Sheets node.\n2. Create a Zoom Marketplace webhook app, point it at this webhook URL, subscribe to one recording event and enable the download token.\n3. Paste your Zoom secret token into **Sign Validation Token**.\n4. Connect Google Sheets, Gmail and OpenAI.\n5. Set coach name and nudge limits in **Set Nudge Rules**, then activate."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "5f36dd9e-8569-4528-81ad-9ecf5ce70840",
      "name": "Section - Zoom Intake & Verification",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -256,
        -144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 948,
        "height": 780,
        "content": "## Zoom Intake & Verification\nZoom checks the endpoint with a signed challenge before sending events, and the validation branch answers it. Recording events are acknowledged right away so Zoom doesn't retry; anything else is ignored."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "095ba566-3dce-412e-b5d8-6a91e86f32bc",
      "name": "Section - Identify Client",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        720,
        64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 940,
        "height": 536,
        "content": "## Identify Client\n**Clients tab:** Client ID, Client Name, Client Email, Zoom Meeting ID, Coach Email, Goals, Status. Matches on meeting ID, then on client name in the meeting topic. Sessions already logged are skipped."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "63cc3bb9-aecd-4043-a63a-0a3510757492",
      "name": "Section - Get the Transcript",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1696,
        -32
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 900,
        "height": 692,
        "content": "## Get the Transcript\nUses Zoom's audio transcript when it exists. Otherwise the audio goes to Whisper, which caps files at 25 MB (roughly 45 minutes of M4A), so turn on Zoom transcripts for longer sessions."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "fc4dacad-c82e-4245-abb9-acbeb6ed2302",
      "name": "Section - Action Plan & Delivery",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2640,
        96
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1536,
        "height": 472,
        "content": "## Action Plan & Delivery\nGPT writes the recap and homework, the client gets an HTML email and everything is logged.\n**Session Log:** Session ID, Client ID, Client Name, Session Date, Duration, Summary, Homework Count, Progress Score, Next Session Focus."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "fec81a3c-0586-495a-aad1-9f9b66c7ac2c",
      "name": "Section - Pick Who to Nudge",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -256,
        784
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 940,
        "height": 380,
        "content": "## Pick Who to Nudge\nRuns daily at 10 AM and groups open tasks due soon or a little overdue, so each client gets one email.\n**Homework Tracker:** Task ID, Client ID, Client Name, Client Email, Session Date, Task, Why, Due Date, Status, Nudge Count, Last Nudge Date."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "3167aab7-7de5-4a2b-8c7d-1ebc1f072c72",
      "name": "Section - Send & Log Nudges",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        704,
        816
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1136,
        "height": 356,
        "content": "## Send & Log Nudges\nGPT drafts a short, encouraging check-in that mentions progress so far. After sending, each task's nudge count and date are updated. Set a task's Status to Done to stop reminders."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "55a0d6eb-b350-4add-aca9-980aae7f425e",
      "name": "Credentials & Security",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
